-- Fraud Act 2006 (2006 c. 35), section 9: PARTICIPATING IN FRAUDULENT BUSINESS CARRIED ON BY
-- SOLE TRADER ETC.
--
-- Section 9 catches a person who is knowingly a party to carrying on a business with intent to
-- defraud creditors or for another fraudulent purpose, where the business is carried on by a
-- person OUTSIDE the reach of section 993 of the Companies Act 2006 (fraudulent trading).
-- Section 993 and section 1(1) of the Companies Act 2006 are not among the sources, so who is
-- within the reach of section 993, and what a "fraudulent purpose" is (section 9(5)), are facts
-- the person states.  A company that is carried on fraudulently is therefore NOT within section
-- 9: it is within section 993 (finding 11 in NOTES.md).
--
-- Section 9(4) is blank in this text (a row of dots), and section 10 (the penalty for fraudulent
-- trading by a company) is blank too; both are quoted at the foot of this file.

§ `Participating in fraudulent business (section 9)`

-- src:77 | 9 Participating in fraudulent business carried on by sole trader etc.
-- src:78 | (1) A person is guilty of an offence if he is knowingly a party to the carrying on of a business to which this section applies.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 9(1) (src:78)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Fraudulent business case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` `the case` MEANS
        `the case`'s `knowingly a party to the carrying on of the business`
    AND `section 9(2): the business is one to which section 9 applies` `the case`

-- src:79 | (2) This section applies to a business which is carried on—
-- src:80 | (a) by a person who is outside the reach of section 993 of the Companies Act 2006 (offence of fraudulent trading), and
-- src:81 | (b) with intent to defraud creditors of any person or for any other fraudulent purpose.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 9(2) (src:79-81)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Fraudulent business case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 9(2): the business is one to which section 9 applies` `the case` MEANS
        `section 9(2)(a): the business is carried on by a person outside the reach of section 993` `the case`
    AND `section 9(2)(b): the business is carried on with intent to defraud creditors or for another fraudulent purpose` `the case`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 9(2)(a) (src:80)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Fraudulent business case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 9(2)(a): the business is carried on by a person outside the reach of section 993` `the case` MEANS
    NOT (`section 9(3): the business is carried on by a person within the reach of section 993` `the case`)

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 9(2)(b) (src:81)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Fraudulent business case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 9(2)(b): the business is carried on with intent to defraud creditors or for another fraudulent purpose` `the case` MEANS
        `the case`'s `the business is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of any person`
    OR  `the case`'s `the business is carried on for any other fraudulent purpose (as in section 993)`

-- src:82 | (3) The following are within the reach of that section—
-- src:83 | (a) a company (as defined in section 1(1) of the Companies Act 2006);
-- src:84 | (b) a person to whom that section applies (with or without adaptations or modifications) as if the person were a company;
-- src:85 | (c) a person exempted from the application of that section.
-- src:86 | (4) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:87 | (5) “Fraudulent purpose” has the same meaning as in that section.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 9(3) and (5) (src:82-85) (src:87)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `Fraudulent business case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 9(3): the business is carried on by a person within the reach of section 993` `the case` MEANS
    -- (a) a company (as defined in section 1(1) of the Companies Act 2006); (b) a person to whom
    -- section 993 applies, with or without adaptations or modifications, as if the person were a
    -- company; (c) a person exempted from the application of section 993.  Section 9(5): a
    -- "fraudulent purpose" has the same meaning as in section 993; that meaning is not in the
    -- sources, so whether the purpose is fraudulent is asked as a fact.
        `the case`'s `the business is carried on by a company (as defined in section 1(1) of the Companies Act 2006)`
    OR  `the case`'s `the business is carried on by a person to whom section 993 applies as if the person were a company`
    OR  `the case`'s `the business is carried on by a person exempted from the application of section 993`

-- src:88 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:89 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or to both);
-- src:90 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or to a fine (or to both).
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 9(6) (src:88-90)
GIVEN place IS A Place
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`section 9(6): the penalty for participating in fraudulent business carried on by sole trader etc.` place `the date the offence was committed` MEANS
    `the penalty subsection: what may follow conviction` 10 place `the date the offence was committed`

-- Section 9(7) (Northern Ireland reads the limit as 6 months) is stated once, with its four
-- twins, in fraud-penalty.l4.

§§ `Blank in this text: section 9(4) and section 10`

